# Book $ Notes Vault

A personal reading tracker built with vanilla HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.
No frameworks used.

## Live Demo
https://kamikazililian236.github.io/Books-Vaults/

## Features
- Add, edit, and delete book records with cover images
- Dashboard with total books, total pages, and weekly additions
- Live search with regex support and match highlighting
- Filte books by tag and reading status
- Sort books by title or date added
- Reading goal tracker with ARIA live region updates
- JSON import and export with validation
- Fully responsive across mobile, tablet, and desktop
- Keyboard navigation and skip-to-content link

## Regex Catalog

| Rule | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| Title | `/^[A-Za-z0-9]+(?:[ -][A-Za-z0-9]+)*$/` | Rejects leading spaces |
| Pages | `/^[1-9]\d*$` | only positive integers |
| Date | `/^d{4}-(0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(0[1-9]|[12]\d|3[01])$/` | YYYY-MM-DD only |
| Duplicate words (Advanced) | `/\b(\w+)\s+\1\b/i` | catches "Library Library" |

## Keyboard Map
- `Tab` - Move between elements
- `Enter` / `Space` -Activate buttons
- `Escape` - Close mobile drawer

## Accessibility Notes
-All inputs have visible labels
-ARIA live region on reading goal tracker
-Skip to main content link present
-Mobile drawer has aria-label

